&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style="font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em;"&gt;
&lt;div&gt;    
&lt;table border=0 cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0 border=0 cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0&gt;&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td align="left" style="padding-left: 4px; font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em;"&gt;&lt;p&gt;#​806 — October 13, 2026&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td align="right" style="padding-right: 4px; font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em;"&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://javascriptweekly.com/link/191505/rss" style=" color: #3366aa;"&gt;Read on the Web&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;

&lt;table border=0 cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0 border=0 cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style=" font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em;"&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;

&lt;table border=0 cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0 border=0 cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style="font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0 12px;"&gt;&lt;p&gt;JavaScript Weekly&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;
&lt;table border=0 cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0 border=0 cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style="font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em;"&gt;
&lt;a href="https://javascriptweekly.com/link/191449/rss" style=" color: #3366aa;"&gt;&lt;img src="https://res.cloudinary.com/cpress/image/upload/w_1280,e_sharpen:60,q_auto/m1xxxsvconnhew26d4uh.jpg" width="640" style="    line-height: 100%;    "&gt;&lt;/a&gt;
&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;

&lt;table border=0 cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0 border=0 cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style="font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 15px;"&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-weight: 600; font-size: 1.1em; color: #000;"&gt;&lt;a href="https://javascriptweekly.com/link/191449/rss" title="deno.com" style=" color: #3366aa;    font-size: 1.1em; line-height: 1.4em;"&gt;Deno is Joining Cloudflare (But…)&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt; — Maybe David Bushell &lt;a href="https://javascriptweekly.com/link/191450/rss" style=" color: #3366aa;   "&gt;saw the writing on the wall&lt;/a&gt;, as the Deno team isn't joining Cloudflare to keep working on &lt;em&gt;Deno&lt;/em&gt;, but to fold &lt;a href="https://javascriptweekly.com/link/191451/rss" style=" color: #3366aa;   "&gt;celld&lt;/a&gt; into &lt;code&gt;workerd&lt;/code&gt; so Durable Objects can be self-hosted (&lt;a href="https://javascriptweekly.com/link/191506/rss" style=" color: #3366aa;   "&gt;more on that here&lt;/a&gt;). The Deno runtime will get a final year of official fixes, Deno Deploy closes in six months, and &lt;a href="https://javascriptweekly.com/link/191452/rss" style=" color: #3366aa;   "&gt;JSR&lt;/a&gt; moves to Cloudflare's infrastructure.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Ryan Dahl &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;
&lt;table border=0 cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0 border=0 cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style="font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 15px;"&gt;&lt;p&gt;💡 &lt;a href="https://javascriptweekly.com/link/191453/rss" style=" color: #3366aa; font-weight: 500;"&gt;On Hacker News&lt;/a&gt;, Ryan Dahl noted that Deno &lt;em&gt;"has been sucked into the gravity well of Node compatibility"&lt;/em&gt; before asking: &lt;em&gt;"Why reimplement Node? It works."&lt;/em&gt; But what happens &lt;a href="https://javascriptweekly.com/link/191454/rss" style=" color: #3366aa; font-weight: 500;"&gt;to the JavaScript™ trademark case&lt;/a&gt;, I wonder…?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;

&lt;table border=0 cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0 border=0 cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style="font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 15px;"&gt;
&lt;a href="https://javascriptweekly.com/link/191448/rss" style=" color: #3366aa;   "&gt;&lt;img src="https://res.cloudinary.com/cpress/image/upload/c_limit,w_480,h_480,q_auto/copm/f0a41815.png" width="135" height="135" style="padding-top: 12px; padding-left: 12px;     line-height: 100%; "&gt;&lt;/a&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-weight: 600; font-size: 1.1em; color: #000;"&gt;&lt;a href="https://javascriptweekly.com/link/191448/rss" title="agentfield.ai" style=" color: #3366aa;    font-size: 1.05em;"&gt;CodeAF: #1 of Ten Coding Harnesses on DeepSWE&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt; — Ten coding harnesses ran the same open model on 113 real GitHub issues. CodeAF solved the most and paid the least per solved issue: 3.4x less than Claude Code, 4.8x less than OpenCode. A new open-source coding harness built for open models.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;AgentField AI &lt;span style="text-transform: uppercase; margin-left: 4px; font-size: 0.9em;   color: #993 !important; padding: 1px 4px; "&gt;sponsor&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;

&lt;table border=0 cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0 border=0 cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style="font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 15px;"&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-weight: 600; font-size: 1.1em; color: #000;"&gt;&lt;a href="https://javascriptweekly.com/link/191455/rss" title="bun.com" style=" color: #3366aa;    font-size: 1.05em;"&gt;Bun 1.4.3 Adds &lt;code&gt;bun check&lt;/code&gt;, a Built-In TypeScript Type Checker&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt; — &lt;code&gt;bun check&lt;/code&gt; is a port of TypeScript 7's checker that reads your &lt;code&gt;tsconfig.json&lt;/code&gt;, reports the same errors as &lt;code&gt;tsc&lt;/code&gt; and, Jarred claims, runs 3-6x faster. It plugs into &lt;code&gt;bun run&lt;/code&gt;/&lt;code&gt;test&lt;/code&gt;/&lt;code&gt;build&lt;/code&gt; too. Idle server processes now use far less CPU, and a JavaScriptCore upgrade picks up &lt;a href="https://javascriptweekly.com/link/191456/rss" style=" color: #3366aa;   "&gt;numerous perf gains&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Jarred Sumner &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;
&lt;table border=0 cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0 border=0 cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style="font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 15px;"&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;IN BRIEF:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;AWS has launched &lt;a href="https://javascriptweekly.com/link/191457/rss" style=" color: #3366aa; font-weight: 500;   "&gt;Lambda Web Functions&lt;/a&gt;, which run an ordinary port-listening Node server (Express, Hono, Fastify, etc.) on Lambda with no handler rewrite, billing for active CPU time and separately for memory.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;📊 The &lt;a href="https://javascriptweekly.com/link/191458/rss" style=" color: #3366aa; font-weight: 500;   "&gt;2026 &lt;em&gt;Stack Overflow&lt;/em&gt; Developer Survey results&lt;/a&gt; are out (30,903 people took part) with JavaScript the #1 language for the 12th year in a row (and TypeScript at #6).&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;🔒 Despite this week's &lt;a href="https://javascriptweekly.com/link/191459/rss" style=" color: #3366aa; font-weight: 500;   "&gt;fresh stir&lt;/a&gt;, no malicious Zod release reached npm. &lt;a href="https://javascriptweekly.com/link/191460/rss" style=" color: #3366aa; font-weight: 500;   "&gt;Malicious commits pushed to its repo in September&lt;/a&gt; were reverted the same day, as &lt;a href="https://javascriptweekly.com/link/191461/rss" style=" color: #3366aa; font-weight: 500;   "&gt;Colin McDonnell explains&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;🔒 &lt;a href="https://javascriptweekly.com/link/191462/rss" style=" color: #3366aa; font-weight: 500;   "&gt;An out-of-band Next.js security release is due tomorrow&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;
&lt;table border=0 cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0 border=0 cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style="font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 15px;"&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;RELEASES:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Last second addition:&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;a href="https://javascriptweekly.com/link/191508/rss" style=" color: #3366aa; font-weight: 500;   "&gt;TanStack Start 1.0&lt;/a&gt; has just dropped. Big news for full-stack React and Solid fans! :-)&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;🎉 &lt;a href="https://javascriptweekly.com/link/191463/rss" style=" color: #3366aa; font-weight: 500;   "&gt;Partytown 1.0&lt;/a&gt; – A popular way to relocate third-party scripts to run in a Web Worker rather than on the main thread has left beta after five years in development.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://javascriptweekly.com/link/191464/rss" style=" color: #3366aa; font-weight: 500;   "&gt;Marionette 5.0&lt;/a&gt; – Six years on, the Backbone-era framework returns with a core free of Backbone, jQuery and Underscore… and they explain why!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://javascriptweekly.com/link/191507/rss" style=" color: #3366aa; font-weight: 500;   "&gt;Bootstrap 6 Alpha&lt;/a&gt; – An early look at Bootstrap's first major release since 2021, leaning on modern CSS and making its JavaScript plugins ESM-only.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://javascriptweekly.com/link/191465/rss" style=" color: #3366aa; font-weight: 500;   "&gt;Express 5.3.0&lt;/a&gt; – A maintenance release worth upgrading to, as patched &lt;code&gt;qs&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;proxy-addr&lt;/code&gt; and &lt;code&gt;body-parser&lt;/code&gt; dependencies close five CVEs.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;
&lt;table border=0 cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0 border=0 cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style="font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0;"&gt;&lt;p&gt;📖  Articles and Videos&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;
&lt;table border=0 cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0 border=0 cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style="font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em;"&gt;
&lt;a href="https://javascriptweekly.com/link/191466/rss" style=" color: #3366aa;"&gt;&lt;img src="https://res.cloudinary.com/cpress/image/upload/w_1280,e_sharpen:60,q_auto/gacrsvr1mipjqdooocro.jpg" width="640" style="    line-height: 100%;      "&gt;&lt;/a&gt;
&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;

&lt;table border=0 cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0 border=0 cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style="font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 15px;"&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-weight: 600; font-size: 1.1em; color: #000;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;📊&lt;/span&gt; &lt;a href="https://javascriptweekly.com/link/191466/rss" title="lemire.me" style=" color: #3366aa;    font-size: 1.05em;"&gt;WebSocket Servers in JavaScript: Node.js, Bun, and Deno&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt; — In 2023, &lt;a href="https://javascriptweekly.com/link/191467/rss" style=" color: #3366aa;   "&gt;Daniel found Bun much faster&lt;/a&gt; than Node at relaying WebSocket messages, but there was a bug in his Bun server. This new attempt uses a C client/relay as a baseline, and Node 26 now gets close to C latency, ahead of Bun and Deno.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Daniel Lemire &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;

&lt;table border=0 cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0 border=0 cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style="font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 15px;"&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-weight: 600; font-size: 1.1em; color: #000;"&gt;&lt;a href="https://javascriptweekly.com/link/191468/rss" title="sindresorhus.com" style=" color: #3366aa;    font-size: 1.05em;"&gt;How Sindre Sorhus' Personal Site is Now Made in Swift&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt; — One of JavaScript's most prolific developers explains how he's dropped Astro and now builds his personal site with Swift, including the styling and markup, with broken links and style typos failing at compile time (&lt;a href="https://javascriptweekly.com/link/191469/rss" style=" color: #3366aa;   "&gt;source&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Sindre Sorhus &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;

&lt;table border=0 cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0 border=0 cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style="font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 15px;"&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-weight: 600; font-size: 1.1em; color: #000;"&gt;&lt;a href="https://javascriptweekly.com/link/191470/rss" title="sentry.io" style=" color: #3366aa;    font-size: 1.05em;"&gt;Too Many Agent Traces to Read? Find the Ones That Matter, Live Oct 14&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt; — Bad answers, wrong tool calls, too many traces. See how Sentry engineers find the failures worth fixing. &lt;a href="https://javascriptweekly.com/link/191470/rss" style=" color: #3366aa;   "&gt;Register now&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Sentry &lt;span style="text-transform: uppercase; margin-left: 4px; font-size: 0.9em;   color: #993 !important; padding: 1px 4px; "&gt;sponsor&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;

&lt;table border=0 cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0 border=0 cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style="font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 15px;"&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-weight: 600; font-size: 1.1em; color: #000;"&gt;&lt;a href="https://javascriptweekly.com/link/191471/rss" title="www.raymondcamden.com" style=" color: #3366aa;    font-size: 1.05em;"&gt;Tiny Apps with TinyJS&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt; — A quick look at &lt;a href="https://javascriptweekly.com/link/191472/rss" style=" color: #3366aa;   "&gt;a new way to make tiny JS-powered desktop apps&lt;/a&gt; we featured a few weeks ago.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Raymond Camden &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;
&lt;table border=0 cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0 border=0 cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style="font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 15px;"&gt;
&lt;p&gt;📄 &lt;a href="https://javascriptweekly.com/link/191473/rss" style=" color: #3366aa; font-weight: 500;   "&gt;Yet Another Way to Invoke Functions Without Parentheses&lt;/a&gt; – There are many ways to invoke arbitrary functions in JavaScript &lt;em&gt;without&lt;/em&gt; using parens, but this is a particularly obscure one! &lt;cite&gt;bartosz&lt;/cite&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;📄 &lt;a href="https://javascriptweekly.com/link/191474/rss" style=" color: #3366aa; font-weight: 500;   "&gt;Six Months of Building with Remix 3&lt;/a&gt; – What the post-React Remix (v3 was released earlier this month) is like to work with day to day. &lt;cite&gt;Sergio Xalambrí&lt;/cite&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;📄 &lt;a href="https://javascriptweekly.com/link/191475/rss" style=" color: #3366aa; font-weight: 500;   "&gt;A Visual Notation for React's Parent and Owner Trees&lt;/a&gt; – With &lt;a href="https://javascriptweekly.com/link/191476/rss" style=" color: #3366aa; font-weight: 500;   "&gt;a playground&lt;/a&gt; that draws them from your code. &lt;cite&gt;Jules Blom&lt;/cite&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;📄 &lt;a href="https://javascriptweekly.com/link/191477/rss" style=" color: #3366aa; font-weight: 500;   "&gt;How to Test an &lt;code&gt;iframe&lt;/code&gt;'s &lt;code&gt;postMessage&lt;/code&gt; Handler&lt;/a&gt; &lt;cite&gt;Keshav Malik&lt;/cite&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;
&lt;table border=0 cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0 border=0 cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style="font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0;"&gt;&lt;p&gt;🛠 Code &amp;amp; Tools&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;
&lt;table border=0 cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0 border=0 cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style="font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em;"&gt;
&lt;a href="https://javascriptweekly.com/link/191478/rss" style=" color: #3366aa;"&gt;&lt;img src="https://res.cloudinary.com/cpress/image/upload/w_1280,e_sharpen:60,q_auto/yyyvmcrgd42zwknefp1s.jpg" width="640" style="    line-height: 100%;      "&gt;&lt;/a&gt;
&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;

&lt;table border=0 cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0 border=0 cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style="font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 15px;"&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-weight: 600; font-size: 1.1em; color: #000;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;🤖&lt;/span&gt; &lt;a href="https://javascriptweekly.com/link/191478/rss" title="anoma.ly" style=" color: #3366aa;    font-size: 1.05em;"&gt;OpenCode 2.0: A Big Update for the Open Coding Agent&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt; — A full-featured agentic coding app, built on Bun, that's more akin to &lt;em&gt;Claude Code&lt;/em&gt; than &lt;a href="https://javascriptweekly.com/link/191479/rss" style=" color: #3366aa;   "&gt;Pi&lt;/a&gt;, say. v2.0 overhauls it with background subagents, a 'code mode' to let models script MCP tool calls, and clients for vanilla JS and Effect code to drive it.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Anomaly / The OpenCode Team &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;
&lt;table border=0 cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0 border=0 cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style="font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 15px;"&gt;&lt;p&gt;💡 If you've not given OpenCode a try yet, you can &lt;a href="https://javascriptweekly.com/link/191480/rss" style=" color: #3366aa; font-weight: 500;"&gt;get started here&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;

&lt;table border=0 cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0 border=0 cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style="font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 15px;"&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-weight: 600; font-size: 1.1em; color: #000;"&gt;&lt;a href="https://javascriptweekly.com/link/191484/rss" title="tamagui.dev" style=" color: #3366aa;    font-size: 1.05em;"&gt;Tamagui 3: One React UI Codebase for Web and Native&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt; — A styling system and component kit for sharing UI between React web apps and React Native, with a compiler that keeps things fast on both. v3 adds Tailwind-style props and React Strict DOM support.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Nate Wienert &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;

&lt;table border=0 cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0 border=0 cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style="font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 15px;"&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-weight: 600; font-size: 1.1em; color: #000;"&gt;&lt;a href="https://javascriptweekly.com/link/191483/rss" title="try.expo.dev" style=" color: #3366aa;    font-size: 1.05em;"&gt;Mobile AI Infrastructure for Web Devs Who Code with Agents&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt; — Point the agent you use for the web at iOS and Android. Expo takes care of the native builds and the trip to the stores.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Expo &lt;span style="text-transform: uppercase; margin-left: 4px; font-size: 0.9em;   color: #993 !important; padding: 1px 4px; "&gt;sponsor&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;

&lt;table border=0 cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0 border=0 cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style="font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 15px;"&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-weight: 600; font-size: 1.1em; color: #000;"&gt;&lt;a href="https://javascriptweekly.com/link/191481/rss" title="h3.dev" style=" color: #3366aa;    font-size: 1.05em;"&gt;H3 v2: The UnJS HTTP Framework Rebuilt on Web Standards&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt; — The minimal HTTP framework behind Nitro and Nuxt's server layer is now stable in v2, a rewrite around standard &lt;code&gt;Request&lt;/code&gt; and &lt;code&gt;Response&lt;/code&gt; so the same app runs on Node, Bun, Deno, Workers, and even in the browser. &lt;a href="https://javascriptweekly.com/link/191482/rss" style=" color: #3366aa;   "&gt;Migration guide&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Pooya Parsa &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;

&lt;table border=0 cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0 border=0 cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style="font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 15px;"&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-weight: 600; font-size: 1.1em; color: #000;"&gt;&lt;a href="https://javascriptweekly.com/link/191485/rss" title="shaders.com" style=" color: #3366aa;    font-size: 1.05em;"&gt;Shaders: 190+ WebGPU Effect Components, Now Open Source&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt; — Ripples, glows, and dissolves into ASCII, composed as components rather than written as shader code, for React, Vue, Svelte, Solid, or plain JS. The engine, framework bindings, and &lt;a href="https://javascriptweekly.com/link/191486/rss" style=" color: #3366aa;   "&gt;the components themselves&lt;/a&gt; are now all MIT licensed.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Simon Le Marchant &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;
&lt;table border=0 cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0 border=0 cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style="font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 15px;"&gt;&lt;p&gt;💡 If you like this vibe, &lt;a href="https://javascriptweekly.com/link/191487/rss" style=" color: #3366aa; font-weight: 500;"&gt;ascii.rest&lt;/a&gt;, which offers &lt;em&gt;"236 animated ASCII pieces for web pages"&lt;/em&gt;, is also worth a look.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;
&lt;table border=0 cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0 border=0 cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style="font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 15px;"&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://javascriptweekly.com/link/191488/rss" style=" color: #3366aa; font-weight: 500;   "&gt;Node.js v26.11.0 (Current)&lt;/a&gt; – Adds a &lt;code&gt;--process-timeout&lt;/code&gt; flag to end a process after a set time, plus virtual table support in &lt;code&gt;node:sqlite&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://javascriptweekly.com/link/191489/rss" style=" color: #3366aa; font-weight: 500;   "&gt;Hono 5.0 RC&lt;/a&gt; – The web-standards server framework goes ESM-only and moves its runtime adapters into separate packages.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;🔒 &lt;a href="https://javascriptweekly.com/link/191490/rss" style=" color: #3366aa; font-weight: 500;   "&gt;Handlebars 4.7.10&lt;/a&gt; – The templating library fixes two critical JavaScript injection flaws affecting releases back to 3.0.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://javascriptweekly.com/link/191491/rss" style=" color: #3366aa; font-weight: 500;   "&gt;he 2.0&lt;/a&gt; – Robust HTML entity encoder/decoder. First release in eight years, now ESM with named exports.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://javascriptweekly.com/link/191492/rss" style=" color: #3366aa; font-weight: 500;   "&gt;React Aria 1.22&lt;/a&gt; – Adds a new &lt;a href="https://javascriptweekly.com/link/191493/rss" style=" color: #3366aa; font-weight: 500;   "&gt;Sheet component&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://javascriptweekly.com/link/191494/rss" style=" color: #3366aa; font-weight: 500;   "&gt;pnpm 12.12&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;
&lt;table border=0 cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0 border=0 cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style="font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px;"&gt;
&lt;table border=0 cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0 border=0 cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style=" font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em;"&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;

&lt;table border=0 cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0 border=0 cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style="font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 15px;"&gt;
&lt;p&gt;📰 Classifieds&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;
&lt;table border=0 cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0 border=0 cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style="font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 15px;"&gt;
&lt;p&gt;⚡️Add lightning-fast 1D/2D barcode scanning to your web app with &lt;a href="https://javascriptweekly.com/link/191495/rss" style=" color: #3366aa; font-weight: 500;   "&gt;STRICH&lt;/a&gt;. On-device processing, &lt;a href="https://javascriptweekly.com/link/191495/rss" style=" color: #3366aa; font-weight: 500;   "&gt;free trial and demo!&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Durable AI agents built with the AI SDK you already use. Long-lived LLM sessions that survive deploys, crashes &amp;amp; refreshes. &lt;a href="https://javascriptweekly.com/link/191496/rss" style=" color: #3366aa; font-weight: 500;   "&gt;Test out chat.agent on Trigger.dev&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;🎬 Your app needs video, not a video team. Upload any format to &lt;a href="https://javascriptweekly.com/link/191497/rss" style=" color: #3366aa; font-weight: 500;   "&gt;Hyperserve's API&lt;/a&gt;, get back MP4 on a global CDN. Ship video in an afternoon.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;
&lt;table border=0 cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0 border=0 cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style=" font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em;"&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;
&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;
&lt;table border=0 cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0 border=0 cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style="font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0;"&gt;&lt;p&gt;📢  Elsewhere in the ecosystem&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;
&lt;table border=0 cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0 border=0 cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style="font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 15px;"&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In &lt;a href="https://javascriptweekly.com/link/191498/rss" style=" color: #3366aa; font-weight: 500;   "&gt;Fingerprints are the New Cookies&lt;/a&gt;, Roy Fish demonstrates the various ways web pages can assign a unique(ish) identity to you using JavaScript.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;🤖 Theo Browne set AI agents loose on porting the TypeScript 7 compiler to Rust, and &lt;a href="https://javascriptweekly.com/link/191499/rss" style=" color: #3366aa; font-weight: 500;   "&gt;ts-rust&lt;/a&gt; is the (very experimental) result.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;📱 Following Shopify, &lt;a href="https://javascriptweekly.com/link/191500/rss" style=" color: #3366aa; font-weight: 500;   "&gt;Coinbase is moving its app off React Native&lt;/a&gt;, saying agents have made building each feature twice cheap enough to go fully native.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Fancy a retro robot voice in your web experience? &lt;a href="https://javascriptweekly.com/link/191501/rss" style=" color: #3366aa; font-weight: 500;   "&gt;Klattsch&lt;/a&gt; is a voice synthesizer you can use on the web or from Node.js as an npm package. &lt;em&gt;Daiiisy, daiiisy…&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Three years ago we mentioned Linus Groh's Zig-based &lt;a href="https://javascriptweekly.com/link/191502/rss" style=" color: #3366aa; font-weight: 500;   "&gt;Kiesel&lt;/a&gt; JavaScript engine. It passed 25% of test262 back then, but &lt;a href="https://javascriptweekly.com/link/191503/rss" style=" color: #3366aa; font-weight: 500;   "&gt;v0.4.0 has landed&lt;/a&gt; and it's now at 94.7% (not far behind V8) and supports modern language proposals like await dictionary and numerous iterator proposals.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;
&lt;table border=0 cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0 border=0 cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style=" font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em;"&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/table&gt;




